  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It seems like if your client lags behind a world for too long, you desynchronize from the timestep and end up seeing a slow motion version of all actions being done by all other players. \n\nThey still see and hear you in proximity, but all updates stop occurring in realtime on your client. You'll see a frame-by-frame update of their positions, as if time has slowed to 1/60th to 1/100th of actual time.\n\nWhile I've had this happen personally, I've also seen others have the same glitch, with one happening on stream. \n\nhttps://clips.twitch.tv/BeautifulAggressiveMacaroniCclamChamp",
